{"name":"Empire Gold","hex":"#c19f6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"empire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A political state, often a monarchy, that has achieved a much greater current size than its initial size by conquering surrounding territories, cities or nations.","A political unit ruled by an emperor or empress."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Empire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empire"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Empire","blocks":[{"text":"An empire is a group of territories controlled by a monarch or a supreme central authority. Within an empire, different populations may have different sets of rights and may be governed differently. The word \"empire\" derives from the Roman concept of Imperium, which refers to the right to command. Empires have taken many forms throughout history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Modern_Empires.svg/330px-Modern_Empires.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/33